TASK:{"title":"AERO9500 Final Report (Part 2): Space Mission Design","overview":"Develop a preliminary space-mission design that benefits Australia and report the mission concept and its space-segment elements. Use mission-design software of your choice, supported by hand calculations if useful, and justify the proposed design."}
RUBRIC:[{"id":"C1","name":"Introduction: mission concept and rationale. Include the following required information: What is the spacecraft's primary mission? Why is the mission needed? How many spacecraft are used and why? Who are the users (operator and customers)?","weight":10,"max":null,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Addresses all requirements to a high standard. Detailed descriptions and discussions are included. References to literature as appropriate."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Addresses some requirements. Descriptions may feature lack of specific details and/or incomplete referencing."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"Many or all requirements are not addressed. Poor descriptions or lack of appropriate referencing."}]},{"id":"C2","name":"Main body: mission design. Present a summary of the mission design using software and/or hand calculations as appropriate. Include relevant screenshots and software files in the main body of the report and/or appendix. Include the following information: Where will it launch from, and using which launch vehicle? Why did you choose this option? What type of orbit will you use? What are its characteristics and orbital elements? Will you need to perform any orbital maneuvers? Which ground control facilities will you use? How often will your spacecraft be able to communicate with ground control? How long will the mission last, and what are your plans for EOL?","weight":60,"max":null,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Demonstrates high level understanding of the design procedure. Design clearly addresses mission and course concepts. Major requirements are all addressed and are well supported with quality evidence (e.g. software screenshots, software files, hand calculations, references from literature). Content is comprehensive, accurate, and persuasive."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Demonstrates adequate understanding of the design procedure. Design may be inconsistent with regards to purpose and clarity of thought or feature errors. Major requirements are addressed but may lack some detail or are not well supported with evidence. Content may not be comprehensive and/or persuasive."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"Demonstrates minimal understanding of the design procedure. Major requirements are not addressed and/or lack evidence. Content is incomplete or not persuasive."}]},{"id":"C3","name":"Conclusion","weight":10,"max":null,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Detailed and appropriate conclusions reached from the evidence provided in the report."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Some conclusions are reached but they may be generic or lack specific detail."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"No actual or useful conclusions reached."}]},{"id":"C4","name":"Report presentation","weight":20,"max":null,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The document follows a clear and logical engineering report structure. The report is easy to read: well-written, with good spelling and grammar, and appropriate language style. All aspects of formatting are consistent throughout the document. Executive summary (or abstract) provides a concise overview of the report. Graphical and tabular presentation of data is appropriate, clear and consistent. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are cited properly."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Document is not at a professional level but does make use of headings and subheadings to indicate document structure. The report may be difficult to read: writing is just ok, broad idea comes across; spelling and grammar have some flaws, not quite appropriate language style. Although figures and tables are labelled, the formatting is unclear and/or inconsistent to the extent that the reader can lose track of the context when reading. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are mostly cited correctly."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"The document is poorly structured, is not coherent or shows a lack of understanding of the purpose of its sections. Much effort is required to read and understand the report: writing is poor, many mistakes with spelling and grammar, and possibly inappropriate language style (e.g. too informal). Presentation is poor to the extent that it impedes reading of the document. Examples include inconsistent formatting, and unlabelled figures or tables. References are either not cited or cited inconsistently."}]}]
MARKING:{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","met":"yes","where":"Introduction"},{"id":"R2","met":"yes","where":"Introduction - 'Thus, only one satellite is required.'"},{"id":"R3","met":"yes","where":"Introduction - CSIRO/BOM users, government/university funding"},{"id":"R4","met":"yes","where":"Mission Design - Launch (Vega E, Guiana Space Centre)"},{"id":"R5","met":"yes","where":"Mission Design - Orbit (COE table: a=6971km, e=0, i=97.79°)"},{"id":"R6","met":"yes","where":"Orbit - 'the only orbital manoeuvre occurs at the EOL segment'"},{"id":"R7","met":"yes","where":"Ground Control & Communications (Mt Pleasant, STK access summary)"},{"id":"R8","met":"yes","where":"Mission Duration & EOL (5 years, drag sail)"},{"id":"R9","met":"yes","where":"STK simulations and MATLAB inclination-vs-altitude plot"},{"id":"R10","met":"partial","where":"Screenshots included (Images 1-5, access report) but no explicit STK scenario files or appendix provided"},{"id":"R11","met":"partial","where":"Structure is clear, but Wikipedia is cited and references are bare URLs without proper citation format"}],"technical_issues":[{"where":"Mission Design - Orbit","issue":"'A very high altitude would yield low resolution images which is also desirable' – contradiction; low resolution is undesirable for reef imaging."},{"where":"Mission Design - Orbit","issue":"RAAN of 27.33° claimed to 'indicate the location of the launch facility'; Kourou is at ~52°W and RAAN is not set by launch-site longitude."},{"where":"Mission Duration & EOL","issue":"Contradictory paragraph: satellite 'without thrusters' yet discusses choosing uncontrolled descent, then restates it has no thrust capability; drag-sail sentence is incomplete."},{"where":"Bibliography","issue":"Wikipedia used as a source, which the task explicitly disallows; references lack titles/authors/access dates."},{"where":"Ground Control & Communications","issue":"Claim that vertical inclination 'maintains a significant contact for the vast majority of passes' is vague and unsupported; access table shows duplicated access number 13."}],"overall":"A well-motivated Australian reef-monitoring CubeSat-style mission with sound SSO selection, STK access analysis and EOL planning. Main weaknesses are internal contradictions, a questionable RAAN justification, missing STK files, and sub-professional referencing (Wikipedia, bare URLs) and figure/table labelling.","criteria":[{"id":"C1","level":"Accomplished","mark":8.0,"scale":10.0,"points":8.0,"max":10.0,"reasoning":"All required elements addressed: primary mission (fluid-lensing reef monitoring), rationale with bleaching statistics and references, single-spacecraft justification, and users/funding. Detail is good though user discussion is brief and operator vs customer roles could be sharper.","evidence":[{"where":"Introduction","quote":"Coral reefs, specifically the Great Barrier Reef, would immensely benefit from dedicated satellite monitoring."},{"where":"Introduction","quote":"Thus, only one satellite is required."},{"where":"Introduction","quote":"The proposed satellite would likely be used by governmental and science agencies (e.g. CSIRO, BOM)"}]},{"id":"C2","level":"Accomplished","mark":7.0,"scale":10.0,"points":42.0,"max":60.0,"reasoning":"Launch, orbit (COE table, J2 hand calc plot), manoeuvres, ground station with STK access report, duration and EOL all addressed with screenshots and evidence. Weaknesses: RAAN value incorrectly tied to launch site, contradictory altitude-resolution statement, no explicit STK files/appendix, EOL discussion muddled.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Design - Launch","quote":"The proposed satellite will thus use the Vega E rocket as a launch vehicle – launched from the Guiana Space Centre Spaceport."},{"where":"Mission Design - Orbit","quote":"an altitude of 600km requires a mean inclination of 97.7924°"},{"where":"Ground Control & Communications","quote":"Systems Tool Kit 11 (STK) was used to calculate access periods as seen below:"},{"where":"Mission Duration & EOL","quote":"The most promising alternative is a ‘drag sail’"}]},{"id":"C3","level":"Adequate","mark":7.0,"scale":10.0,"points":7.0,"max":10.0,"reasoning":"Conclusions summarise each segment and acknowledge risks (Vega E availability, fallback to Vega C). Reasonably specific but brief; no quantitative recap (e.g. access statistics, orbit elements) and no forward recommendations beyond launch contingency.","evidence":[{"where":"Conclusion","quote":"A specific launch vehicle – the Vega E – has been selected although it has not been built yet."}]},{"id":"C4","level":"Adequate","mark":5.0,"scale":10.0,"points":10.0,"max":20.0,"reasoning":"Structure is logical with headings and executive summary, but figures/tables lack numbers, references are bare URLs including Wikipedia (explicitly disallowed), bibliography entries malformed, and several typos/unfinished sentences ('complied', 'purposed', broken drag-sail sentence). Not professional-level presentation.","evidence":[{"where":"Bibliography","quote":"[6] https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2021_in_spaceflight. [Online]."},{"where":"Orbit","quote":"STK 3D view of orbit: 12 hours apart"},{"where":"Mission Duration & EOL","quote":"utilising a large surface area to ‘ and is suitable for low-earth orbit altitudes"}]}]}
